name: do-not-create-duplicate-ui-components
description: UI/Component Reuse Policy (MANDATORY)
---

# Overview

- Do NOT create duplicate UI components.
- Before creating any new component, ALWAYS search the existing codebase for a similar component.
- Prefer reusing and extending existing components over creating new ones.
- All reusable UI components must live in /src/components/ui or /src/components/shared.
- Feature-specific components must live in /src/features/<feature>/components.
- If a new component is needed, it must be added to the global component library and exported from the component index.
- Every new component must include:
  - a clear name
  - typed props (TypeScript)
  - minimal styling
  - documentation comment describing intended reuse
- Never copy-paste a component to a new folder. Refactor to shared instead.
